VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-id.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=your_supabase_anon_key_here
VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here
VITE_AUTO_LOGIN_EMAIL=test@test.be
VITE_AUTO_LOGIN_PASSWORD=password

# Getting your Gemini API key is a quick process through Google AI Studio. Here are the steps:

# Go to Google AI Studio: Navigate to aistudio.google.com.

# Sign in: Log in with your Google account. (If it's your first time, you may need to accept the terms of service).

# Navigate to API Keys: On the left-hand menu, look for and click on Get API key or API keys.

# Create a Key: Click the Create API key button.

# Select a Project: A dialog will appear asking you to add a key-project pair. If you don't already have a Google Cloud project, Google AI Studio can automatically create a new one for you.

# Copy and Save: Your new API key (a long string of characters) will be generated. Copy it immediately.

# Important Security Note: Treat your API key like a password. Do not paste it directly into code that you plan to upload publicly (like a public GitHub repository). Instead, store it safely in an environment variable (e.g., a .env file) as GEMINI_API_KEY.